   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to authorizing the Flanders, Riverside and Northampton\nCommunity Association, Inc. to file an application for a partial exemption\nfrom real property taxes",
    "basePrintNo": "S6590",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6590-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6590\n\nSPONSOR: PALUMBO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to authorizing the Flanders, Riverside and Northamp-\nton Community Association, Inc. to file an application for a partial\nexemption from real property taxes\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo authorize the assessor of the town of Southampton to accept from\nFlanders, Riverside and Northampton Community Association Inc. and\napplication for a partial exemption from real property tax for the\n2019-2020 assessment roll, for a parcel located at 12 Oaks Avenue in the\ntown of Southampton.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 authorizes the assessor of the town of Southampton to accept\nfrom Flanders, Riverside and Northampton Community Association Inc. a\nretroactive partial real property tax exemption application for the\n2019-2020 assessment roll.\n\nSection 2 provides for an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Flanders, Riverside and Northampton Community Association Inc.\n(FRNCA) acquired twelve parcels of vacant land from the State for the\npurposes of preservation after these lands had been damaged by hurricane\nSandy. FRNCA mistakenly missed the deadline to submit a 420-a applica-\ntion for a partial real property tax exemption for the parcel of land\nlocated at 12 Oaks Avenue in the town of Southampton.  This legislation\nis needed for the assessor to accept the retroactive application.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
